{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"const useIsomorphicLayoutEffect: (effect, deps?) => void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/react-form/src/useIsomorphicLayoutEffect.ts#L3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/react-form/src/useIsomorphicLayoutEffect.ts:3"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The signature is identical to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useEffect"},{"type":"text","value":", but it fires synchronously after all DOM mutations.\nUse this to read layout from the DOM and synchronously re-render. Updates scheduled inside\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLayoutEffect"},{"type":"text","value":" will be flushed synchronously, before the browser has a chance to paint."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefer the standard "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useEffect"},{"type":"text","value":" when possible to avoid blocking visual updates."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you’re migrating code from a class component, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLayoutEffect"},{"type":"text","value":" fires in the same phase as\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"componentDidMount"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"componentDidUpdate"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"effect","children":[{"type":"text","value":"effect"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"EffectCallback"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"deps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"deps?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DependencyList"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"version","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Version"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"16.8.0"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"see","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://react.dev/reference/react/useLayoutEffect","children":[{"type":"text","value":"https://react.dev/reference/react/useLayoutEffect"}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"effect","text":"effect","level":3},{"id":"deps","text":"deps?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"version","text":"Version","level":2},{"id":"see","text":"See","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nconst useIsomorphicLayoutEffect: (effect, deps?) => void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/react-form/src/useIsomorphicLayoutEffect.ts:3](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/react-form/src/useIsomorphicLayoutEffect.ts#L3)\n\nThe signature is identical to `useEffect`, but it fires synchronously after all DOM mutations.\nUse this to read layout from the DOM and synchronously re-render. Updates scheduled inside\n`useLayoutEffect` will be flushed synchronously, before the browser has a chance to paint.\n\nPrefer the standard `useEffect` when possible to avoid blocking visual updates.\n\nIf you’re migrating code from a class component, `useLayoutEffect` fires in the same phase as\n`componentDidMount` and `componentDidUpdate`.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### effect\n\n`EffectCallback`\n\n### deps?\n\n`DependencyList`\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Version\n\n16.8.0\n\n## See\n\n[https://react.dev/reference/react/useLayoutEffect](https://react.dev/reference/react/useLayoutEffect)\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useIsomorphicLayoutEffect\ntitle: useIsomorphicLayoutEffect\n---\n\n```ts\nconst useIsomorphicLayoutEffect: (effect, deps?) => void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/react-form/src/useIsomorphicLayoutEffect.ts:3](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/react-form/src/useIsomorphicLayoutEffect.ts#L3)\n\nThe signature is identical to `useEffect`, but it fires synchronously after all DOM mutations.\nUse this to read layout from the DOM and synchronously re-render. Updates scheduled inside\n`useLayoutEffect` will be flushed synchronously, before the browser has a chance to paint.\n\nPrefer the standard `useEffect` when possible to avoid blocking visual updates.\n\nIf you’re migrating code from a class component, `useLayoutEffect` fires in the same phase as\n`componentDidMount` and `componentDidUpdate`.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### effect\n\n`EffectCallback`\n\n### deps?\n\n`DependencyList`\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Version\n\n16.8.0\n\n## See\n\n[https://react.dev/reference/react/useLayoutEffect](https://react.dev/reference/react/useLayoutEffect)\n"}
